meta {
  name: Crea Accesso per Odonimo Esistente
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workflows/crea-accesso-per-odonimo
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "codcom": "H501",
    "prognaz": "920585",
    "numero_civico": "95",
    "esponente": "A",
    "sezione_censimento": "580911010001"
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

tests {
  test("an already-existing accesso is returned, not duplicated", function() {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.body.progressivo_nazionale_odonimo).to.equal("920585");
    expect(res.body.progressivo_civico).to.be.a("string");
  });
}

docs {
  Add an accesso to an existing odonimo, identified by its national progressive
  (`prognaz`, required; ADR 0020). Existence is checked from that prognaz with the
  AdE accparz `civico[/esponente][-specificità]`: no match -> create; exactly one ->
  return the existing `prognazacc` (no duplicate); more than one -> fail (ambiguous).

  This example hits the "already exists" branch (VIA TARANTO 95/A), so it returns
  the existing prognazacc WITHOUT writing — safe to run. The create branch is a
  WRITE; to exercise it as a no-op, create a clearly-new civic then suppress it
  (sopprimi-accesso), like the "Dry-run Accesso" pair.

  Validated against PDND collaudo (UAT): prognaz 920585, civic 95 esponente A ->
  returns prognazacc 33160578 (the existing 95/A), no creation.
}
